1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,176
Every lie you tell makes you lighter. Tell enough, and you simply float away into the gray sky.

2
00:00:07,476 --> 00:00:13,572
I lied about brushing my teeth this morning, and my left sneaker barely touches the floorboards now.

3
00:00:13,872 --> 00:00:21,168
My mother stays firmly planted downstairs. She claims she never lies. Not even a tiny white one.

4
00:00:21,468 --> 00:00:27,972
I walk down the stairs, gripping the wooden banister tightly so I don't drift into the ceiling.

5
00:00:28,272 --> 00:00:36,024
Mom stands by the kitchen counter, feet flat and heavy, chopping vegetables with steady, solid motions.

6
00:00:36,324 --> 00:00:42,228
I ate the last slice of pie, but I told her the neighbor's dog broke in and stole it.

7
00:00:42,528 --> 00:00:50,304
Mom looks up, sighs, and hands me the heavy iron anchor she keeps ready for my constant dishonesty.

8
00:00:50,604 --> 00:00:56,364
I clutch the iron to my chest, dropping back down to the floor with a dull, heavy thud.

9
00:00:56,664 --> 00:01:03,768
Then she looks me in the eye and drops the heaviest truth of all, shattering everything instantly.

10
00:01:04,068 --> 00:01:09,780
She says she never lied to protect me... except for the biggest one about who I really am.
